## 2026-09-07 route-change and pressure acceptance
Compose existing P3AI navigation, P3TowerDefense combat/wave authority, Earthworks #1012 and placement #1033/#2440. Reuse current #2603 wave-phase WIP.

Test one real lane sequence: baseline creep route -> valid terrain/defense change -> nav/collision update -> alternate route/declared failure -> destruction or undo -> route reopened. Define the pending-update behavior; creeps must not tunnel, attack an unreachable stale Core location, freeze indefinitely or instantly teleport through the obstruction. A final-path rejection/rollback must preserve valid world/economy state.

Core relocation invalidates relevant goals; spawn/defeat and wave pressure remain server-owned. Declare target selection and no-path recovery in current feature data/logic. Do not add a second navigation registry. Local nav generation/invokers are an option only if #2611 identifies the existing generation strategy as a cost problem.

Show both teams' pressure and the player's ability to change it in normal play. Measure edit-to-valid-route latency on the fixed workload; no invented universal timing threshold. Enemy behavior and navigation updates serialize at their actual .cpp owners; scenario/evidence preparation can proceed independently.

---

Parent: #803 / #941.

Make the live Lane War feel like a lane battle rather than a systems sandbox. Reuse the existing creep, faction, navigation, damage and Core authorities; do not create another wave/combat system.

Acceptance:
- both teams continuously create visible lane pressure;
- opposing creeps meet, fight, die and continue toward the enemy Core;
- surviving creeps can damage the Core and player actions can materially change that pressure;
- blockers/terrain changes use the existing navigation behavior instead of bypassing it;
- Core destruction produces the existing replicated match result;
- verify through the normal playable Lane War path, not a new proof harness.

## 2026-09-07 economy decision and tuning acceptance
Recent earn/spend and +1 EXTRA LANE PRESSURE feedback already landed; preserve it and test its actual consequence before adding more labels.

Record a short normal-match baseline: first affordable decision, source of gold, purchase opportunities, creep pressure before/after spend and time until a win/loss opportunity. Compare extra-unit versus upgrade choice at matched initial state; exact tuning remains data-driven. Do not claim balance from UI wording.

Reject duplicate/stale/invalid purchase requests, insufficient gold, terminal-match spending and disconnected-client attempts through the existing authoritative transaction path. Spend and resulting unit/upgrade happen exactly once; rematch resets only declared match state.

Keep earthworks free and map-wide as required by the northstar; do not attach the construction/shop economy to terrain editing. Construction cost and salvage/refund remain their own declared rules.

Use the existing shop/economy/HUD owners. P3TowerDefenseFeatureActor.cpp and P3LaneWarHUDWidget.cpp serialize with #2437/#2440 and other current contributors. Evidence/tuning analysis can proceed without editing those files.

---

Parent: #803 / #941.

Turn the existing Lane War economy into a player decision loop. Reuse current gold, creep-shop and upgrade authority; no new economy framework.

Acceptance:
- gold rises from the intended creep-related play and periodic income;
- the player can clearly see current gold and what can be bought;
- buying an extra allied creep/minion visibly changes lane pressure;
- buying a creep upgrade visibly changes later allied creeps and communicates the new level/effect;
- pacing is playable enough that a normal short match demonstrates earn -> choose -> spend -> visible consequence;
- server authority/replication remain the existing implementation.

## 2026-09-07 movement feel and transition acceptance
Reuse current ski/grapple owners and #2461 proof work; consume #2606 HUD work before overlapping it.

Prove a normal-player route where downhill momentum creates a combat/rotation advantage and uphill/friction/landing respond predictably. Grapple valid/invalid target, release/cancel, obstruction, moving/changed terrain and attack-before/after transitions must leave input and player state coherent. Camera collision/view changes must not hide essential combat or grant an untested view-dependent movement advantage.

#2610 owns animation matching the real velocity/ski/grapple/air/landing state. Do not replace skiing with a dash or solve body pose by changing movement authority. Show server/remote-client behavior under #2442's recorded emulation profile and separate expected prediction correction from gameplay-state divergence.

Use a fixed route and comparable input sequence for before/after feel tuning. Record observed speed/trajectory, lost-control moments and player-visible results; no new movement framework or engine migration without a measured failing requirement.

---

Parent: #803 / #941.

Make high-mobility traversal matter inside the real Lane War. Reuse the existing movement, grapple, camera and input owners; this is gameplay integration/tuning, not a new movement system.

Acceptance:
- momentum skiing/surfing rewards slope and route choice instead of behaving like ordinary running;
- grapple can enter, escape or reposition during live lane combat;
- at least one useful route combines lane terrain/verticality with skiing and grapple;
- movement remains controllable and readable in both first-person and third-person;
- abilities/combat can be used before/after traversal without losing player state or input;
- tune/fix concrete feel problems found in play rather than adding generic movement infrastructure.

## 2026-09-07 placement, destruction and anti-soft-lock contract
Reuse current #1033/#1012, #2605 placement and #2600 rollback WIP. Shared placement/authority files serialize.

The player may choose defenses/Core position, but a valid match must retain declared access/counterplay. Revalidate placement against authoritative terrain/structure state, player/team rights, support/collision and the actual route policy. Handle a terrain change or another placement between preview and server commit; reject/rollback without double cost or stale invisible collision.

Test full blocking attempts, Core relocation during existing creep targeting, destruction during pending nav update, support removal and repeated undo/refund as applicable. Server gameplay health/collision determines access; Chaos debris presentation cannot keep an invisible permanent blocker or award duplicate damage/refund.

Show place -> defend -> enemy counter -> reopened route -> renewed Core pressure through normal controls on both clients. Keep free earthworks separate from construction economy. The final outcome belongs in #803/#941, not a standalone placement demo.

---

Parent: #803 / #941. Compose existing Core relocation plus #1033 construction and existing destruction; do not add another placement or objective system.

Acceptance:
- each player can choose a valid Core position in/around the live base through normal controls;
- the player can place existing walls/defences to make that position meaningfully easier to defend;
- the enemy can attack/destroy defences and reopen access rather than creating a permanent soft lock;
- invalid Core/defence placements fail visibly and preserve a playable route;
- both clients see the same authoritative Core/base state;
- prove the loop as player choice -> build defence -> enemy counterplay -> Core pressure.

## 2026-09-07 readability and accessible feedback
Use the existing P3Combat presentation actors, cues, health read models and HUD. Coordinate animation through #2610, not a second animation controller.

Evaluate at ordinary speed/distance with the selected roster and real meteor/ability set:
- distinguish caster/team, target/danger area, cast versus impact, hit versus miss, invulnerability/block/cooldown where applicable;
- first-person hands/body/effects and third-person camera collision must not obscure aim or essential enemy tells;
- communicate damage direction, health/result and resource/cooldown through readable shape/text/icon/timing as well as color; critical information must not rely on audio or color alone;
- retain useful sound/impact cues but avoid repeated cue spam or effects that hide Core/creep/contact state;
- expose existing sensitivity, camera/FOV and readability settings coherently where supported; do not turn this into a settings framework.

Capture one attacker/observer sequence in each view and record concrete unreadable moments before tuning. Profile expensive VFX only if #2611 identifies the cost. P3CombatMeteorPresentationActor.cpp, P3CombatHUDWidget.cpp and P3LaneWarHUDWidget.cpp each serialize independently with current claimants.

---

Parent: #803 / #941. Coordinate with #956 and #1091. Reuse current P3Combat, spell, GameplayCue/VFX, health and HUD presentation owners; no new presentation framework.

Acceptance:
- the important live abilities have readable cast/start, travel/active and impact/result feedback where applicable;
- enemy hero/creep damage and defeat are understandable at normal gameplay distance and speed;
- cooldown/resource feedback is visible enough to make combat decisions without reading logs;
- first-person and third-person both remain usable and do not hide essential tells;
- fix concrete missing/weak cues found in a normal Lane War play pass using existing assets where practical.
